and Candy Apples

00:03:52.850 --> 00:03:55.440
Ah! Onee-chan will be getting home soon!

00:03:55.880 --> 00:03:58.150
I have to start preparing breakfast.

00:04:06.920 --> 00:04:08.350
I’m finally done.

00:04:09.060 --> 00:04:14.520
Looking for

00:04:09.060 --> 00:04:14.520
a small puppy

00:04:09.060 --> 00:04:14.520
Fireworks

00:04:09.060 --> 00:04:14.520
Festival

00:04:09.510 --> 00:04:14.520
Now that I think about it, last year, Asu was the one who really looked forward to the fireworks festival.

00:04:14.920 --> 00:04:16.560
But this year…

00:04:21.180 --> 00:04:22.150
Okay!

00:04:26.280 --> 00:04:29.740
That’s right! The change from yesterday’s grocery shopping.

00:04:37.520 --> 00:04:40.890
I’m counting on you. I’ve saved up little by little just for this day.

00:04:42.270 --> 00:04:45.680
Onee-chan and I are going to have a lot of fun at the food stands.

00:04:46.140 --> 00:04:47.550
Candy apples,

00:04:47.550 --> 00:04:48.910
takoyaki,{melody capitalizes this, wry?}

00:04:48.910 --> 00:04:50.690
and rice crackers with sauce.{“senbei” a specific type of Japanese rice crackers, but doremi just goes with: “Japanese crackers”}

00:04:53.320 --> 00:04:54.400
I’m home!

00:04:55.180 --> 00:04:56.710
Onee-chan, welcome home!

00:04:58.810 --> 00:05:00.740
Thank you for your hard work.

00:05:00.740 --> 00:05:02.530
Breakfast is ready.

00:05:02.910 --> 00:05:04.990
Thanks for the food!

00:05:10.400 --> 00:05:12.550
Today’s the day of the fireworks festival!

00:05:12.550 --> 00:05:14.890
Yeah, it really is!

00:05:15.980 --> 00:05:20.080
Hey, after I finish cleaning, may I go out for a little bit?

00:05:20.080 --> 00:05:22.510
That’s fine. It is Sunday, after all.

00:05:22.510 --> 00:05:23.840
But where are you going?

00:05:24.950 --> 00:05:26.880
You’ll find out later.

00:05:29.740 --> 00:05:31.370
I’m going now!

00:05:32.900 --> 00:05:35.780
Next-door neighbor, your mailbox is full!{yeah, no, it still sounds retarded, but I won’t stand for “neighbor-san”, better suggestions desired}

00:05:37.370 --> 00:05:39.030
It’s really full!{don’t shout too loudly now, Asu}

00:05:40.770 --> 00:05:43.030
Asu! Be careful, okay?

00:05:43.030 --> 00:05:44.530
I know!

00:05:44.530 --> 00:05:46.700
Hey, seriously, where are you going?

00:05:46.970 --> 00:05:48.650
You’ll find out later.

00:05:50.560 --> 00:05:53.940
Ah, Mr. Landlord, good morning.

00:05:56.060 --> 00:05:57.790
Well then, me too.

00:06:14.360 --> 00:06:15.100
Yes!{orig: All right!}{my translation: “hai!”}

00:06:19.480 --> 00:06:21.980
Good morning, Asu!

00:06:19.480 --> 00:06:21.980
I can't wait for today's

00:06:19.480 --> 00:06:21.980
fireworks festival!

00:06:19.480 --> 00:06:21.980
Kyou

00:06:19.480 --> 00:06:21.980
I can't wait for today's

00:06:19.480 --> 00:06:21.980
fireworks festival!

00:06:25.880 --> 00:06:26.900
Go!

00:06:31.400 --> 00:06:33.990
Well, if it isn’t Asu-chan!

00:06:33.990 --> 00:06:36.500
Hey, it’s Yaoichi’s husband.

00:06:36.920 --> 00:06:39.260
Are you going to be selling vegetables at this stand today?

00:06:40.570 --> 00:06:42.850
Vegetables wouldn’t sell too well at a festival.

00:06:42.850 --> 00:06:43.630
Ah! These are…

00:06:43.980 --> 00:06:46.590
Yeah, we’re going to be a candy apple stand today.

00:06:46.910 --> 00:06:49.430
Really? A candy apple stand?

00:06:49.730 --> 00:06:52.160
My sister and I will come by later to buy one!

00:06:52.160 --> 00:06:55.630
Okay! Then I’ll prepare an extra large one just for you.

00:06:56.190 --> 00:06:57.730
Thank you very much!

00:06:59.610 --> 00:07:05.260
There’s the yakisoba stand, the shooting game stand, and the cotton candy stand.

00:07:13.430 --> 00:07:14.990
It’s done{complete}!

00:07:22.820 --> 00:07:24.010
Ma’am!

00:07:27.910 --> 00:07:29.470
I’m home!

00:07:30.500 --> 00:07:33.310
Huh? Onee-chan?

00:07:42.200 --> 00:07:44.310
T-The money is…

00:07:55.710 --> 00:07:57.280
Asu, I’m home!

00:07:57.820 --> 00:08:00.250
Sorry I’m so late.

00:08:01.290 --> 00:08:03.470
What’s wrong? The lights aren’t even on.

00:08:08.350 --> 00:08:10.880
Here, Asu, it’s a present.

00:08:11.710 --> 00:08:12.680
A yukata…

00:08:13.310 --> 00:08:14.070
Yes!

00:08:18.170 --> 00:08:19.660
Where’d you get this?{orig: Why do you have this?}

00:08:19.660 --> 00:08:21.730
I bought it at the Hashimoto clothing store.

00:08:22.270 --> 00:08:26.560
I have Mom’s hand-me-down yukata, but you don’t have one.

00:08:26.560 --> 00:08:29.780
I’ve been wanting to get you one as a present for a while now.

00:08:30.230 --> 00:08:34.180
Don’t tell me… You used the money in the piggy bank?

00:08:34.180 --> 00:08:36.660
That’s right. Hurry up and try it on!

00:08:43.600 --> 00:08:44.610
I don’t want it.

00:08:45.160 --> 00:08:48.630
Why? I bought this for you, Asu.

00:08:48.630 --> 00:08:52.120
Why did you spend the money by yourself?{on y’own}

00:08:52.120 --> 00:08:55.430
What do you mean, “why”? I thought you’d like it.

00:08:56.640 --> 00:09:00.210
Hey, we can always save the money back up.

00:09:00.760 --> 00:09:04.870
Okay, it’s my fault for spending the money without asking you.

00:09:04.870 --> 00:09:09.510
But since the day’s here, put on your new yukata
and we’ll go to the fireworks festival, okay?

00:09:10.430 --> 00:09:11.480
I’m not going.

00:09:11.890 --> 00:09:13.630
Who cares about the fireworks festival?

00:09:14.030 --> 00:09:15.450
I’m not going!

00:09:17.440 --> 00:09:19.060
Onee-chan, you idiot!

00:09:29.700 --> 00:09:31.470
<i>I saved that money for so long,</i>

00:09:31.470 --> 00:09:34.240
<i>just so we could spend it together at the fireworks festival.</i>

00:09:34.880 --> 00:09:38.140
<i>The takoyaki stand. The rice cracker stand, too…</i>

00:09:38.140 --> 00:09:41.350
<i>Everything that I was waiting for!</i>

00:09:41.820 --> 00:09:45.260
<i>I really wanted us to eat a big candy apple together!</i>

00:09:46.850 --> 00:09:47.760
Asu…

00:09:56.540 --> 00:09:58.540
I’m going to return this yukata.

00:10:01.950 --> 00:10:10.000
The Yamada family's slightly
luxurious dandelion coffee.

00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:18.470
A bargain sale,
such a glorious sight.

00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:18.470
Bargain Sale

00:10:22.210 --> 00:10:23.130
Rain…

00:10:24.710 --> 00:10:26.390
I have to go look for Asu!

00:10:29.410 --> 00:10:30.580
Last time…

00:10:30.940 --> 00:10:32.860
It’s the same as last time.{HOORAY FOR CONTRIVED CONFLICT}

00:10:44.020 --> 00:10:45.800
Barely made it!

00:10:46.700 --> 00:10:49.170
Asu! Asu?

00:10:49.600 --> 00:10:51.490
She’s not home yet…

00:10:51.900 --> 00:10:54.740
I wonder if she’s okay. Maybe she’s still at school.

00:10:54.740 --> 00:10:57.620
If she’s outside, I hope she found shelter from the rain.{I hope she’s not out in the rain, maybe?}

00:11:01.680 --> 00:11:04.030
I hate thunder!

00:11:07.440 --> 00:11:10.730
<i>What if Asu’s also…{orig: What if… Asu is also…?}</i>

00:11:13.990 --> 00:11:15.490
Hang in there, Asu.

00:11:15.490 --> 00:11:17.810
Your older sister is coming to get you!{perhaps “alright?” or “okay?” for “ne”}

00:11:21.550 --> 00:11:24.970
The lightning—it hit somewhere nearby.{needs split/retime}

00:11:24.970 --> 00:11:29.760
Oh yeah, I think someone told me that lightning is attracted to umbrellas.

00:11:41.770 --> 00:11:42.920
Onee-chan!

00:11:43.930 --> 00:11:46.720
Onee-chan! Over here! I’m over here!

00:11:48.080 --> 00:11:53.810
<i>Come to think of it, Asu wasn’t afraid of the thunder at all.</i>

00:11:56.580 --> 00:11:58.010
I’m so pathetic.

00:12:01.150 --> 00:12:06.990
That time, I was so scared of the thunder that when I went to get Asu, I almost gave up halfway.

00:12:07.440 --> 00:12:08.710
Today, too…

00:12:10.120 --> 00:12:15.130
Maybe Asu doesn’t even need a sister like me.{alt: Asu might not need a sister like me.}

00:12:18.340 --> 00:12:20.160
Oh my, Asu-chan.

00:12:20.770 --> 00:12:21.800
What’s wrong?

00:12:22.400 --> 00:12:24.760
You’re completely soaked!{and that yukata you’re carrying has unfixable water damage that renders it worthless!}

00:12:25.160 --> 00:12:27.260
What if you catch a cold?{I am marking this for editing but will probably forget to fix it}

00:12:29.040 --> 00:12:30.980
Ma’am, this yukata—

00:12:30.980 --> 00:12:33.920
Oh, this yukata? You like it, right?

00:12:34.950 --> 00:12:37.940
It has the same design as your sister’s.

00:12:38.400 --> 00:12:39.460
The same?

00:12:39.840 --> 00:12:43.900
That’s why she wouldn’t accept anything else.{alt: Kyo-chan wanted this design no matter what.}

00:12:43.900 --> 00:12:46.670
She even went to our warehouse to search for it.

00:12:47.080 --> 00:12:49.970
She probably spent the whole day looking.

00:12:50.540 --> 00:12:52.540
The whole day?

00:12:53.470 --> 00:12:59.720
She probably felt bad because you’ve never had a yukata to wear.

00:13:01.160 --> 00:13:06.630
<i>She went to all that trouble just to find a matching yukata for me?</i>

00:13:07.390 --> 00:13:08.850
<i>For me…</i>

00:13:09.490 --> 00:13:14.450
She was looking forward to wearing matching yukatas and watching the fireworks together.

00:13:14.450 --> 00:13:15.960
It’s okay.

00:13:15.960 --> 00:13:18.350
It’s just drizzling, so it’ll stop soon.

00:13:19.740 --> 00:13:20.450
<i>Rain…</i>

00:13:21.390 --> 00:13:22.540
<i>Just like before.</i>

00:13:24.780 --> 00:13:26.620
<i>The day I forgot my umbrella.</i>

00:13:31.530 --> 00:13:33.220
Ah, more lightning.

00:13:33.660 --> 00:13:35.860
Aww, this is inconvenient.

00:13:35.860 --> 00:13:37.930
I’ll get home late.

00:13:39.640 --> 00:13:41.240
Onee-chan?!

00:13:43.090 --> 00:13:45.570
Onee-chan! Over here! I’m right over here!

00:13:48.120 --> 00:13:50.500
Onee-chan, you came to pick me up?

00:13:51.590 --> 00:13:54.350
But it looks like the rain has stopped.

00:13:56.690 --> 00:14:00.090
You didn’t even use your umbrella, did you?

00:14:04.010 --> 00:14:07.200
<i>Onee-chan hates thunder, but she braved it to come.</i>

00:14:09.880 --> 00:14:12.050
Since you brought them, let’s use them anyway.

00:14:12.050 --> 00:14:14.710
What? That’s embarrassing!

00:14:16.970 --> 00:14:19.080
All that and yet…

00:14:19.350 --> 00:14:21.040
<i>Onee-chan, you idiot!</i>

00:14:22.110 --> 00:14:25.300
I… keep causing trouble for my sister.

00:14:26.240 --> 00:14:30.270
Kyou is always looking out for you, right?

00:14:30.270 --> 00:14:31.960
I told her she was stupid.

00:14:32.540 --> 00:14:36.730
After all she’s done for me, I called her an idiot.

00:14:37.110 --> 00:14:38.070
I…

00:14:40.620 --> 00:14:43.460
It’s all right, Asu.

00:14:44.250 --> 00:14:46.240
I’m not sure what happened,

00:14:46.750 --> 00:14:50.410
but your sister worked hard searching for this yukata.

00:14:50.990 --> 00:14:53.680
Why don’t you wear it and show it to her?

00:14:55.010 --> 00:14:56.860
O-Onee-chan…

00:15:08.580 --> 00:15:09.670
Onee-chan?!

00:15:10.550 --> 00:15:11.780
She’s not here.

00:15:15.430 --> 00:15:16.410
The fireworks…

00:15:25.330 --> 00:15:26.820
Asu!

00:15:30.020 --> 00:15:31.320
Asu!

00:15:41.570 --> 00:15:43.130
<i>Beautiful!</i>

00:15:44.440 --> 00:15:46.970
Tamaya! Kagiya!

00:15:44.440 --> 00:15:51.930
Tamaya and Kagiya were famous rival fireworks manufacturers. At displays, People would root for their favorite—now, shouting their names is just tradition.{localization: FYUCK YEAR FIERWARKS!!!1}

00:15:48.940 --> 00:15:51.930
Every year, Asu and I always watch them together.

00:15:51.930 --> 00:15:53.750
There’s no point if I’m alone.{alt: Watching them alone is meaningless.}

00:15:54.950 --> 00:15:58.340
Even so, I expected Asu to be here.{I thought Asu would be here.}

00:15:58.340 --> 00:15:59.770
Hey, Kyou!

00:16:00.680 --> 00:16:02.480
You came just in time.

00:16:02.480 --> 00:16:05.400
Your special candy apple is almost done.

00:16:05.400 --> 00:16:06.770
Grandpa Yaoichi!

00:16:07.150 --> 00:16:09.790
Asu was really looking forward to it.{this is terrible. I want to put something like “…so excited for toay” or something}

00:16:09.790 --> 00:16:11.990
She said she’d come with her sister.

00:16:11.990 --> 00:16:13.610
What? Asu said that?{Asu? Really? <- this may be a better choice, just for variety}

00:16:13.610 --> 00:16:14.460
Yeah.

00:16:14.460 --> 00:16:18.580
She came to see what stands there were, saying she wanted to escort you around the festival.

00:16:18.720 --> 00:16:19.440
What?

00:16:20.680 --> 00:16:21.710
She did?!

00:16:25.540 --> 00:16:26.960
This memo…

00:16:28.720 --> 00:16:32.240
Asu… she scouted out a plan so she could escort me around.

00:16:34.740 --> 00:16:36.430
For me…

00:16:37.410 --> 00:16:39.680
Why did you spend the money by yourself?

00:16:40.410 --> 00:16:42.140
Who cares about the fireworks festival?

00:16:42.680 --> 00:16:43.810
I’m not going!

00:16:46.280 --> 00:16:48.030
I’m so stupid.

00:16:50.250 --> 00:16:51.450
So stupid!

00:16:54.450 --> 00:16:57.310
Here, it’s done! Your special candy apple!

00:16:57.310 --> 00:16:59.950
Huh? Kyou-chan?

00:17:01.570 --> 00:17:05.060
<i>Asu wanted to enjoy the festival with me,</i>

00:17:05.410 --> 00:17:09.210
<i>but I didn’t understand her feelings.</i>

00:17:09.600 --> 00:17:10.920
<i>Her feelings.{orig: I threw her feelings away… <- way too long for the spoken line. I concur.}</i>

00:17:13.200 --> 00:17:16.640
<i>I promised Mom that I’d take good care of Asu.</i>

00:17:17.390 --> 00:17:18.620
<i>I promised her.</i>

00:17:23.770 --> 00:17:25.060
Excuse me.

00:17:25.980 --> 00:17:27.220
Please let me through.

00:17:29.680 --> 00:17:30.620
Quickly…{it’s entirely fucking unclear whether she’s saying this or just thinking it. The mouth movements could be either mouthbreathing while running or speaking. Even though the words aren’t coming out as though she’s breathing heavily, which lends itself to the theory that she’s thinking, I doubt this show would pay that much attention to detail, and since the mouth movements are non-uniform, I think it can be assumed she is supposedly saying these lines aloud.}

00:17:30.620 --> 00:17:34.810
I have to find Onee-chan quickly, before the fireworks are over.

00:17:36.010 --> 00:17:36.940
Where is she?

00:17:37.700 --> 00:17:40.000
Onee-chan!

00:17:42.210 --> 00:17:43.220
Asu?

00:17:46.170 --> 00:17:46.960
Asu…

00:17:47.280 --> 00:17:48.330
Asu is here!

00:17:59.040 --> 00:18:02.190
Asu!{should be em dash?}

00:18:04.820 --> 00:18:05.810
Onee-chan?

00:18:07.590 --> 00:18:09.450
Asu!

00:18:12.220 --> 00:18:13.570
Onee-chan!

00:18:13.570 --> 00:18:15.530
Asu!

00:18:16.720 --> 00:18:18.630
Onee-chan…

00:18:30.790 --> 00:18:32.970
Onee-chan, I…

00:18:33.580 --> 00:18:36.050
I… I…

00:18:36.740 --> 00:18:39.500
Thank you. You wore the yukata.{alt: Thank you for wearing the yukata.}

00:18:40.670 --> 00:18:42.300
Onee-chan…

00:18:43.490 --> 00:18:44.820
Ah, the fireworks!

00:18:47.130 --> 00:18:50.480
Asu, we were able to watch the fireworks{together} again this year.

00:18:52.610 --> 00:18:53.190
Yeah.

00:18:54.170 --> 00:18:56.120
We got to see them again this year.

00:18:56.120 --> 00:18:57.150
Yep.

00:19:37.150 --> 00:19:38.400
Won’t you rest a little?

00:19:38.750 --> 00:19:42.090
Asu! Why are you here? Go home!

00:19:43.050 --> 00:19:45.730
Onee-chan, I want to work too!{WHY DO WE KEEP DOING GODDAMN SHOWS ABOUT CHILD LABOR}

00:19:46.420 --> 00:19:50.410
You don’t have to worry about money.{orig: You can leave the question of money up to me.}

00:19:50.410 --> 00:19:53.360
I’ll keep working harder and harder.

00:19:53.360 --> 00:19:54.610
It’s all right.

00:19:54.610 --> 00:19:56.340
I’ll just get another job.

00:19:56.340 --> 00:19:57.390
It’s not that.

00:19:58.380 --> 00:19:59.350
Onee-chan.

00:20:02.290 --> 00:20:03.790
Don’t leave me behind.{the gap is too long. It just looked weird lowercase.}

00:20:04.340 --> 00:20:07.060
Don’t disappear like Dad did.{daddy would fit better with otou-chan, not otou-san… that said, she is supposed to be 9}

00:20:09.270 --> 00:20:12.830
I called you stupid, but even so…

00:20:13.370 --> 00:20:15.730
Please, don’t leave me!

00:20:21.360 --> 00:20:22.330
Okay.

00:20:23.940 --> 00:20:26.580
Onee-chan is right here.

00:20:27.550 --> 00:20:29.340
I won’t go anywhere.

00:20:33.270 --> 00:20:34.680
It’s all right.

00:20:35.220 --> 00:20:36.430
Onee-chan!

00:20:39.110 --> 00:20:44.060
<i>Asu, it’s okay. Your sister won’t go anywhere.</i>

00:20:44.980 --> 00:20:50.230
<i>Kyou, you don’t have to worry about not working hard enough.</i>

00:20:51.430 --> 00:21:00.680
<i>The only thing I was able to leave behind for you two was a small promise, but it’s protecting you dearly.{while I agree with that… No idea how to reword to make it not retarded}{idea: The only thing I was able to leave behind for you two was a small promise, but it’s protecting you dearly.}</i>

00:21:00.680 --> 00:21:05.950
<i>One day, when you can’t summon the strength…</i>

00:21:10.310 --> 00:21:11.330
The sun…{STARING AT THE SUN IS BAD FOR YOUR EYES}

00:21:12.250 --> 00:21:13.680
Isn’t it pretty?

00:21:13.680 --> 00:21:14.430
Yeah.

00:21:14.870 --> 00:21:21.000
My promise somehow protects the bonds between you two.{ending this with a semicolon just looked wrong}

00:21:21.000 --> 00:21:24.500
I will always keep this promise.{orig: I will always… keep this promise.}{what the fuck does “I continue to wish it” even mean. Also, fuck ellipsis overuse.}

